@* The site's own layout already has a main element, and a page has only one: As="div" here.
   Class="min-h-48" replaces the viewport-high minimum so the frame stays small. *@
<div class="w-full overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-(--blux-border)">
    <BxHeader Title="Acme" Sticky="false" />
    <BxMain As="div" Class="min-h-48 p-6" data-testid="main">
        <p class="text-sm text-(--blux-text-muted)">
            In a layout, BxMain grows to fill the screen below the header, so the footer never floats up on a short page.
        </p>
    </BxMain>
    <BxFooter>
        <Left><p>Copyright 2026 Acme Inc.</p></Left>
    </BxFooter>
</div>
